     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi all, please consider the data and plot generated by this code:<br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">ggplot2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>df </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">frame</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rnorm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">20</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rnorm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">20</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                 </span><span style=\"color:#008\">group</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;IFNa&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;IFNb&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> each </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">50</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>ggplot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> df</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> aes</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> facet_wrap</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(~</span><span style=\"color:#008\">group</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> geom_point</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span></div></code></div><br>Instead of IFNa and IFNb, I would like the titles to read IFN<span>α and IFN</span><span>β. I have tried using:<br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> facet_wrap</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(~</span><span style=\"color:#008\">group</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><code><span style=\"color:#000\"> labeller </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> label_parsed</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></code></div></code></div></span><span><br>but I&#39;m not sure what format my group labels should be in. I tried the format:<br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">paste</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;IFN&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;alpha&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>but this didn&#39;t work. Can anyone please suggest a way to do this and combine standard latin text and greek letters in my facet_wrap titles?<br><br>Thank you<br>Hefin<br></span></div>"
    ]
   ]
